# Every failed login (unknown identifier, wrong password, a customer's identifier) answers the same 401 problem
# (title invalid_credentials), sets no cookie and never says which part was wrong. A disposable mechanic is the known account.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@TestPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_PASSWORD}}
@TestWrongPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WRONG_PASSWORD}}
@AdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@AdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@KnownCustomerEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_CUSTOMER_EMAIL}}
@RunId = {{$timestamp}}
# Phone digits derived from this run's id so the registration never collides with another file or an earlier, aborted run.
@PhoneTail = {{RunId.toString().slice(-6)}}
@KnownMechanicEmail = login.negmatrix.known.{{RunId}}@example.test


### [Setup][Auth] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Admin Session] Login as admin to provision the known mechanic (200 expected)
# @name Login
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{AdminEmail}}", "password": "{{AdminPassword}}" }

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('__Host-arsm-csrf-token='))?.match(/^__Host-arsm-csrf-token=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Register] Known mechanic with an email and a phone (200 expected)
# @name knownMechanic
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "NegMatrix", "lastName": "Known", "email": "{{KnownMechanicEmail}}", "password": "{{TestPassword}}", "personType": "Mechanic", "phoneNumber": "+36 30 3{{PhoneTail}}", "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel", "expertise": ["Engine"] }

?? status == 200

###

### [Negative][Login] Known account with a wrong password, by email (401 expected, no cookie)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{KnownMechanicEmail}}", "password": "{{TestWrongPassword}}" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true
?? js (!response.headers['set-cookie']) == true

###

### [Negative][Login] The right password with one character appended is wrong (401 expected)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{KnownMechanicEmail}}", "password": "{{TestPassword}}-wrong" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true

###

### [Negative][Login] Known account with a wrong password, by phone (401 expected)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phoneNumber": "06 30 3{{PhoneTail}}", "password": "{{TestWrongPassword}}" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true

###

### [Negative][Login] Unknown email answers the same problem (401 expected, no cookie)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "login.negmatrix.unknown.{{RunId}}@example.test", "password": "{{TestPassword}}" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true
?? js (!response.headers['set-cookie']) == true

###

### [Negative][Login] Unknown but well-formed phone answers the same problem (401 expected)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phoneNumber": "+49 151 12345678", "password": "{{TestPassword}}" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true

###

### [Negative][Login] A customer's email is not a login (401 expected)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{KnownCustomerEmail}}", "password": "{{TestPassword}}" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true

###

### [Negative][Login] A customer's phone is not a login (401 expected)
# @no-cookie-jar
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "phoneNumber": "+36 30 444 5566", "password": "{{TestPassword}}" }

?? status == 401
?? js response.parsedBody.title == invalid_credentials
?? js (response.parsedBody.detail === "Invalid login credentials.") == true

###

### [Setup][Cleanup] Delete the known mechanic (200 expected)
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{knownMechanic.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Cleanup] Logout the admin session (204 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 204
